      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Warm-up protocol applies.** The first burst after any deploy is a transient: on a freshly created Aurora cluster the same load cost **22x more `DBLoad`** and **152x more pool-wait**, producing an 18.9 s tail that fell to 0 by the third run. **Discard the first burst after any deploy, then measure** \u2014 and state warm-up state alongside any number taken from these panels.\n\n**Saturation is read as queueing, not utilization.** `ACUUtilization` is *capacity / configured capacity*; with the cluster pinned at min = max = 2 ACU it reads a constant 100% and carries no information. Read DB saturation from `DBLoadRelativeToNumVCPUs` (threshold 1.0) and pool saturation from `BorrowLatency`.\n\n**Gaps are not zeros.** Performance Insights metrics publish *only while there is load*, so idle windows are absent datapoints rather than zero values."
      },
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "DB load vs capacity \u2014 Aurora saturation",
      "description": "Average Active Sessions against the vCPU line. The instance presents 1 vCPU at 2 ACU, so DBLoadRelativeToNumVCPUs crossing 1.0 means the database is oversubscribed. DBLoadCPU tracking DBLoad means the load is CPU-class rather than I/O wait.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "efk64tufw3pj4e"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "efk64tufw3pj4e"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/RDS",
          "metricName": "DBLoadRelativeToNumVCPUs",
