    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Little's Law \u2014 L = \u03bbW",
      "description": "L predicted (lambda*W) is plotted against L observed on the SAME axis - that comparison is the point of the panel. Observed running ABOVE predicted is expected: Lambda's Duration measures handler execution only, so time queued ahead of the handler (SnapStart restore, connection setup) inflates observed concurrency without appearing in W. The gap IS the pre-handler cost. Rate and duration sit on the right axis for context; raw invocations-per-minute is hidden because its scale (~10^4) would flatten everything else.",
